name issue_15_aimd_v2_cross_traffic
describe A 1.5 Mbps competing flow joins a 3 Mbps bottleneck at 10 s and leaves at 25 s, `cc v2` (#15)
# Utilization: `cc v1` 64-69 %, `cc v2` 71-79 %, libwebrtc 74.2 % (parity-data, 10 seeds). Queue p95 stays
# under the suite's limit (v2 79-171 ms; libwebrtc 264 ms).
# Port (#150, RobustThroughputEstimator as the acked-rate estimator, as libwebrtc M157): this scenario pinned only `cc v2`, so the
# v1 feedback and recovery stayed in the loop. With the estimator libwebrtc's, the queue rises to libwebrtc's level (262 ms against
# 263.5) and the v1 recovery path froze on 4-5 of 10 seeds (up to 19 freezes) where libwebrtc freezes on 5. It now sets every v2 switch,
# libwebrtc's configuration (#61's flip makes them the default); the expect lines are unchanged.
duration 40s
at 0s  capacity=3000kbps delay=25ms queue=300ms
at 10s cross=1500kbps
at 25s cross=0kbps
expect video.freeze_count == 0
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 250
expect cc.unsettled == 0
expect cc.utilization_pct >= 68
